.TH SWAYDESK-DISPLAYS 1 2026-11-15 "swaydesk 0.1.4" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-displays \- Displays application and screen profile service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-displays
.br
.B swaydesk\-displays daemon
.br
.B swaydesk\-displays apply
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments, a window to arrange the screens of the Sway session: drag them on the map (their edges
snap to each other), and choose, for each one, whether it is on, its resolution, refresh rate, scale
(fractional scales included) and rotation. Identify shows the name of each screen on it. Apply changes the
screens at once and asks whether to keep the change; with no answer in 15 seconds, the previous settings come
back. Keep saves the layout as the profile of the connected set of monitors and writes the Sway file read at
login. Opening it again raises the open window. Its menu entry is org.swaydesktop.Displays.
.PP
Each set of monitors is identified by the make, model and serial number of each one (as in Sway's
\fBoutput "<make> <model> <serial>"\fR), not by the port name. Two identical monitors without a serial number
are told apart by the port.
.PP
With \fBdaemon\fR, the profile service the Sway configuration starts (as sway\-displays daemon, a link in the
package's helper directory): whenever the set of connected monitors changes, or the configuration is
reloaded, it applies the saved profile of the set, if there is one; without one, the screens stay as Sway
chose them. A change made by hand with the same set of monitors is kept until the configuration is
reloaded (swaymsg reload, which the Desktop Theme app also does): then the profile applies again, so a
mode set by hand and not kept in the window is lost. Keep it in the window to make it last. With the laptop lid closed and an
external screen on in the profile, the internal screen stays off. A profile that would turn every screen off
is not applied, and if no screen is on after a change of monitors or a reload, the service turns them all on.
.PP
With \fBapply\fR, it applies the profile of the connected set at once: the Sway configuration runs it when the
laptop lid closes or opens (bindswitch), so closing the lid with an external screen on in the profile turns the
internal screen off, and opening it turns it back on. While the window waits for Keep or Undo, the service does not apply profiles.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The service exits 1 when Sway's event stream ends; the Sway configuration then starts it again while Sway is running.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/displays.json
The profiles: one layout for each set of monitors.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway/config.d/90\-displays.conf
The layout last kept, only the screens that are on, read by Sway at login and on reload (turning a screen
off is left to the service, which knows the set). It comes after 50\-local.conf, so it wins over an output
line there. Written by the window; edits by hand are replaced at the next Keep.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway/outputs
The file of nwg\-displays, still read before config.d, so a layout from it lasts until the first Keep.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR sway\-output (5)
